<section class="page" id="about" data-title="About Us | Covenant Treasures International School" data-desc="Our mission, vision and what the school crest stands for. A Christian school in Ibadan with a multi-dimensional approach to education.">

<section class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>About the school</h1>
    <p>A faith-based school with a multi-dimensional approach, raising future leaders in the tradition of godliness and excellence.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-paper">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <hr class="rule-gold">
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>Covenant Treasures International School is a Christian school in Ibadan, Oyo State, teaching children from
      creche through to college on one campus. We were founded on a simple conviction: that a child's character
      and a child's results are not two separate projects.</p>
    <p>Everything here follows from that. Devotion sits in the timetable alongside mathematics. Teachers are hired
      for what they can draw out of a child, not only for what they know. And parents are treated as partners in
      the work rather than an audience for it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-cream">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid grid--2 reveal reveal-stagger">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Our mission</h3>
        <p>To provide a nurturing and stimulating learning environment that inspires academic excellence,
          builds strong moral values, develops creative and critical thinkers, and equips learners to become
          godly, responsible and impactful leaders in a dynamic world.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Our vision</h3>
        <p>To raise globally minded, confident and compassionate leaders who excel academically, demonstrate
          strong character, embrace innovation, and create a lasting positive impact in their communities and
          the world.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-paper">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <hr class="rule-gold">
      <h2>What the crest means</h2>
      <p>The quartered shield rests on an open book. Each quarter names something we are accountable for.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="quarters reveal reveal-stagger">
  <article class="quarter">
    <div class="mark"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.4 3h5.2v6.4H25v5.2h-6.4V29h-5.2V14.6H7V9.4h6.4V3z" fill="#A8842A"/></svg></div>
    <h3>Faith and character</h3>
    <p>Devotion, scripture and Christian values are woven into the school week, not bolted on at the end of it.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="quarter">
    <div class="mark"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 26 11.5 9l5.2 9.3L20.5 12 30 26H2z" fill="#1B2A4A"/><circle cx="24" cy="6.5" r="3.5" fill="#A8842A"/></svg></div>
    <h3>Academic ambition</h3>
    <p>The Nigerian national curriculum taught to a standard that prepares pupils for WAEC, NECO and beyond.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="quarter">
    <div class="mark"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="none" stroke="#1B2A4A" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M10.5 26V13c0-5-1.2-7-3.7-7S3.3 8.6 4.8 10.7"/><path d="M21.5 26V13c0-5 1.2-7 3.7-7s3.5 2.6 2 4.7"/><path d="M9.5 12.5h13M13.8 13.8v12.2M18.2 13.8v12.2M9.5 27.2h13"/></g></svg></div>
    <h3>Arts and expression</h3>
    <p>Music, drama, choir and public speaking, so every child finds a place where they are confident.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="quarter">
    <div class="mark"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="16" cy="16" r="13" fill="#A8842A"/><path d="M16 3c3.2 3.4 5 8 5 13s-1.8 9.6-5 13c-3.2-3.4-5-8-5-13s1.8-9.6 5-13z" fill="#F8F3EC" opacity=".35"/><path d="M3.6 12h24.8M3.6 20h24.8" stroke="#F8F3EC" stroke-width="1.4" opacity=".45" fill="none"/></svg></div>
    <h3>A wider view</h3>
    <p>Languages, technology and global awareness that let our pupils hold their own anywhere in the world.</p>
  </article>
</div>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-photo">
  <div class="bg bg--basic" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <p class="statement">Excellence, character, leadership &mdash; <em>building a lasting legacy</em> in all we do.</p>
    <p class="attrib">From the school anthem</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-paper">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <hr class="rule-gold">
      <h2>Our core values</h2>
      <p>Six commitments the school measures itself against, in and out of the classroom.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="values reveal reveal-stagger">
      <article class="value"><span class="num">01</span><h3>Excellence</h3>
        <p>Doing ordinary work to an uncommon standard, in the classroom and outside it.</p></article>
      <article class="value"><span class="num">02</span><h3>Integrity</h3>
        <p>Honesty when it costs something. Character is what holds when nobody is checking.</p></article>
      <article class="value"><span class="num">03</span><h3>Discipline</h3>
        <p>The habits that turn ability into achievement, taught patiently and expected consistently.</p></article>
      <article class="value"><span class="num">04</span><h3>Respect</h3>
        <p>For teachers, for one another, and for every family that walks through our gate.</p></article>
      <article class="value"><span class="num">05</span><h3>Leadership</h3>
        <p>Responsibility given early, so pupils learn to carry it before they are asked to.</p></article>
      <article class="value"><span class="num">06</span><h3>Legacy</h3>
        <p>Measuring ourselves by who our pupils become, long after they have left us.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-cream">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="reveal">
        <hr class="rule-gold">
        <h2>Our school anthem</h2>
        <p>Sung at assembly and at every ceremony, it is the shortest statement of what the school is for.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="anthem reveal">
        <h3>Covenant Treasures</h3>
        <p>Covenant Treasures, we proudly stand,<br>
          United in wisdom, heart and hand.<br>
          With truth and excellence, we lead the way,<br>
          Building our future every day.</p>
        <p>Covenant Treasures, our school, our pride,<br>
          With courage and faith, we rise worldwide.<br>
          Excellence, Character, Leadership too,<br>
          Building a lasting legacy in all we do!</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-paper">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <hr class="rule-gold">
      <h2>Leadership</h2>
      <p>The people responsible for the school day to day.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid--3 reveal reveal-stagger">
      <article class="card card--media staff">
        <img src="assets/img/staff/proprietress.webp" alt="Moyosore Somide, Proprietress"
             width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <div class="card-body">
          <p class="meta">Proprietress</p>
          <h3>Moyosore Somide</h3>
          <p>Carries overall responsibility for the school &mdash; its direction, its standards, and the tone
            set from the top. Questions that need a decision rather than an answer come to her.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="card card--media staff">
        <img src="assets/img/staff/head-teacher.webp" alt="The Head Teacher and Head of Academics"
             width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <div class="card-body">
          <p class="meta">Academics</p>
          <h3>Head Teacher &amp; Head of Academics</h3>
          <p>Runs the school day and owns what happens in the classroom: the curriculum across all three
            stages, examination preparation, and the teaching staff. The person to speak to about how your
            child is getting on.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="card card--media staff">
        <img src="assets/img/staff/secretary.webp" alt="The School Secretary"
             width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <div class="card-body">
          <p class="meta">School office</p>
          <h3>School Secretary</h3>
          <p>First point of contact for the school. Handles admissions enquiries, application forms, records
            and fee schedules, and will point you to the right person for anything else.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="cta-band">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <h2>Come and see the school for yourself</h2>
    <p>Book a campus tour on a school day, meet the teachers, and sit in on a lesson. No appointment fee.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn--gold" href="#admissions" data-anchor="apply">Start an application</a>
