<section class="page" id="academics" data-title="Academics | Covenant Treasures International School" data-desc="The Nigerian national curriculum across three stages: creche and nursery, basic school, and college, with WAEC, NECO and JAMB preparation.">

<section class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Academics</h1>
    <p>The Nigerian national curriculum, taught in three stages from creche to college, with the depth to carry a child all the way through.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-paper" id="creche">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <hr class="rule-gold">
        <h2>Creche &amp; Nursery</h2>
        <p class="lede">6 months to 5 years</p>
        <p>The early years are about safety, warmth and curiosity, in that order. Children learn through play,
          songs, stories and structured phonics, in small groups with familiar adults.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>Phonics, early numeracy and handwriting introduced gently and consistently</li>
          <li>Daily routine that covers rest, meals, outdoor play and supervised learning</li>
          <li>Bible stories, memory verses and songs as part of the ordinary day</li>
          <li>Regular updates to parents on how their child is settling</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="figure"><div class="crest-art" aria-hidden="true"></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-cream" id="basic">
  <div class="wrap">
    <hr class="rule-gold">
    <h2>Basic School</h2>
    <p class="lede">Primary 1 to JSS 3</p>
    <p>The Nigerian national curriculum, taught with extra weight on reading, mathematics and ICT because those
      three decide how far a child can go later. Pupils are prepared properly for Common Entrance and the BECE.</p>
    <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <article class="card"><h3>Core subjects</h3><p>English, Mathematics, Basic Science and Technology, National Values, Civic Education and Social Studies.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Beyond the core</h3><p>Computer studies, French, Yoruba, agricultural science, home economics, music and physical education.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Christian studies</h3><p>Weekly scripture, assembly devotion and a character focus that runs through every subject.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-paper" id="college">
  <div class="wrap">
    <hr class="rule-gold">
    <h2>College</h2>
    <p class="lede">SSS 1 to SSS 3</p>
    <p>Three streams, and honest guidance about which one fits a particular student. From SSS 2 the timetable
      turns toward examinations, with structured WAEC, NECO and JAMB preparation rather than last-minute cramming.</p>
    <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <article class="card"><h3>Science</h3><p>Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Further Mathematics and Agricultural Science, with practical laboratory work.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Arts</h3><p>Literature, Government, Christian Religious Studies, History and languages.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Commercial</h3><p>Economics, Financial Accounting, Commerce and Business Studies.</p></article>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:2.5rem">
      <h3>Examination preparation</h3>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Mock examinations under real conditions, marked to WAEC standards</li>
        <li>Registration support for WAEC, NECO and JAMB handled by the school</li>
        <li>One-to-one sessions on course choice, university applications and cut-off marks</li>
        <li>Extra tutorials for students who need them, at no additional charge</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-cream">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <hr class="rule-gold">
    <h2>How we assess</h2>
    <p>Continuous assessment through the term, a mid-term test, and an end-of-term examination. Reports go home
      with a written comment from the class teacher, not only a set of scores, and every parent is invited to a
      termly meeting to go through it.</p>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="cta-band">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <h2>Come and see the school for yourself</h2>
    <p>Book a campus tour on a school day, meet the teachers, and sit in on a lesson. No appointment fee.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn--gold" href="#admissions" data-anchor="apply">Start an application</a>
      <a class="btn btn--onmaroon" href="#contact">Book a tour</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


</section>

<section class="page" id="admissions" data-title="Admissions | Covenant Treasures International School" data-desc="How to apply to Covenant Treasures International School, Ibadan. Five steps, what to bring, fees and answers to common questions.">

<section class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Admissions</h1>
    <p>Open all year for creche and nursery, and at the start of each term for basic school and college.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-paper">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <hr class="rule-gold">
        <h2>How to join us</h2>
        <p>Five steps, and we will walk you through every one of them. Most families finish the process in under
          two weeks.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>
            <h3>Get in touch</h3>
            <p>Send the enquiry form below, call the office, or message us on WhatsApp. Tell us your child's age
              and the class you have in mind.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Visit the school</h3>
            <p>Come on a normal school day. See the classrooms in use, meet the teachers, and ask whatever you
              need to ask. There is no charge for a tour.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Complete the application</h3>
            <p>Collect a form at the office or start online. You will need your child's birth certificate, recent
              passport photographs and the last report card from their current school.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Assessment and interview</h3>
            <p>A short placement assessment for basic school and college entrants, so we put your child in the
              right class. Nursery entrants have an informal chat instead.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Offer and resumption</h3>
            <p>We confirm the offer, share the fee schedule and uniform list, and give you the resumption date
              and everything your child needs on the first day.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>What to bring</h3>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li>Birth certificate or age declaration</li>
            <li>Four recent passport photographs</li>
            <li>Last report card or transfer certificate</li>
            <li>Immunisation record for creche and nursery entrants</li>
            <li>Parent or guardian identification</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card" style="margin-top:1.35rem">
          <h3>Fees</h3>
          <p>Fees vary by stage and are reviewed each session. We would rather discuss them with you directly than
            publish a figure that goes out of date. Call the office or request the current schedule below.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:1rem"><a href="tel:+2349123043411">+234 912 304 3411</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-cream" id="apply">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <hr class="rule-gold">
    <h2>Start an application</h2>
    <p>Fill this in and we will come back to you with the fee schedule, available places and a date for a visit.</p>

    <form class="form" id="enquiry-form" novalidate>
      <div class="two">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="parent">Parent or guardian name</label>
          <input id="parent" name="parent" type="text" autocomplete="name" required>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="phone">Phone number</label>
          <input id="phone" name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" required>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="two">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="email">Email address</label>
          <input id="email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email">
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="child">Child's name</label>
          <input id="child" name="child" type="text">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="two">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="age">Child's age</label>
          <input id="age" name="age" type="text" placeholder="e.g. 7 years">
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="stage">Class applying for</label>
          <select id="stage" name="stage">
            <option value="">Please choose</option>
            <option>Creche</option>
            <option>Nursery</option>
            <option>Primary 1&ndash;6</option>
            <option>JSS 1&ndash;3</option>
            <option>SSS 1&ndash;3</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label for="message">Anything you would like us to know</label>
        <textarea id="message" name="message"></textarea>
      </div>

      <div class="form-note">
        This form opens WhatsApp with your details filled in, so nothing gets lost between your phone and the
        admissions office. You still press send.
      </div>

      <div class="btn-row">
        <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Send my enquiry</button>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="tel:+2349123043411">Call the office instead</a>
      </div>
      <p id="form-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="hint"></p>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-paper">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <hr class="rule-gold">
    <h2>Questions we get asked</h2>
    <div class="acc">
      <div class="acc-item">
        <button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Can my child join in the middle of a term?</button>
        <div class="acc-panel"><p>Usually yes, if there is a place in the class. We will assess where your child is and put support in place so they are not left behind by the transfer.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="acc-item">
        <button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Do you provide transport?</button>
        <div class="acc-panel"><p>Ask the office about the current routes and pickup points. Availability depends on where you live relative to Akala Express Way.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="acc-item">
        <button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Is lunch provided?</button>
        <div class="acc-panel"><p>Speak to the office about the current meal arrangement and any dietary needs your child has.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="acc-item">
        <button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Do you accept children of other faiths?</button>
        <div class="acc-panel"><p>Yes. We are openly a Christian school and devotion is part of our day, and families of every background are welcome as long as they are comfortable with that.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="acc-item">
        <button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">What are the school hours?</button>
        <div class="acc-panel"><p>Confirm current hours with the office, including the after-school arrangement for parents who finish work later.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</section>

<section class="page" id="campus-life" data-title="Campus Life | Covenant Treasures International School" data-desc="24-hour CCTV, reliable power, certified teachers and well-equipped classrooms, plus the clubs, sports and activities that fill the school week.">

<section class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Campus life</h1>
    <p>What a day here actually looks like, and the things we put in place so parents do not have to worry.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-paper">
  <div class="wrap">
    <hr class="rule-gold">
    <h2>Safety comes first</h2>
    <p>Your child's safety is not a feature of the school. It is the condition for everything else in it.</p>
    <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <article class="card"><h3>24-hour CCTV</h3><p>The premises are under continuous camera surveillance, covering classrooms, corridors and the play areas.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Controlled entry</h3><p>Visitors are signed in, and children are released only to a named parent or an authorised guardian.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Reliable power</h3><p>A backup supply keeps lessons, fans and lighting running through outages, so learning is not interrupted.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Certified teachers</h3><p>Every member of teaching staff is qualified, vetted and supported with ongoing training.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Equipped classrooms</h3><p>Spacious, well-ventilated rooms with the materials each stage needs, kept to a manageable class size.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>First aid on site</h3><p>Trained staff and a stocked sick bay, with parents contacted immediately if a child is unwell.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-cream">
  <div class="wrap">
    <hr class="rule-gold">
    <h2>Beyond the classroom</h2>
    <p>Children remember the choir, the match and the debate long after they have forgotten a test.</p>
    <!-- EDIT ME: replace with the clubs and activities the school actually runs. -->
    <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <article class="card"><h3>Choir and music</h3><p>Voice training, instruments and performances at school services and events.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Drama and debate</h3><p>Public speaking and stagecraft, with inter-house and inter-school competitions.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Sports</h3><p>Football, athletics and inter-house sports, culminating in the annual sports day.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>ICT club</h3><p>Typing, basic coding and digital literacy for pupils from upper primary onward.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Press and literary club</h3><p>Writing, reading challenges and the school newsletter.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h3>Excursions</h3><p>Termly educational trips that connect what is taught in class to the world outside it.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-maroon">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <hr class="rule-gold">
    <h2>A day at Covenant Treasures</h2>
    <!-- EDIT ME: confirm the real timetable with the school. -->
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li>Arrival and settling, with staff on the gate to receive every child</li>
      <li>Morning assembly and devotion to open the day together</li>
      <li>Lesson blocks with a mid-morning break</li>
      <li>Lunch and supervised outdoor play</li>
      <li>Afternoon lessons, clubs and activities</li>
      <li>Closing prayer, then a controlled release to parents and guardians</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="cta-band">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <h2>Come and see the school for yourself</h2>
    <p>Book a campus tour on a school day, meet the teachers, and sit in on a lesson. No appointment fee.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn--gold" href="#admissions" data-anchor="apply">Start an application</a>
      <a class="btn btn--onmaroon" href="#contact">Book a tour</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


</section>

<section class="page" id="news" data-title="News and Events | Covenant Treasures International School" data-desc="Term dates, results, competitions and events at Covenant Treasures International School, Ibadan.">

<section class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>News and events</h1>
    <p>Term dates, results, ceremonies and what is happening on campus this session.</p>
